Spec: Android authenticated access Agent

Purpose:
  Run a user-started gateway with Keystore identity, owner approvals and caller-bound Binder streams.

Owns:
  ./build.gradle
  ./src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
  ./README.md

Structure:
  ./src: Owner interface, private foreground runtime and exported authenticated Binder boundary.

References:
  /agent-core/agent-core.sdd
  /transport-core/transport-core.sdd
  /android/control-ipc/control-ipc.sdd

Must:
  Build the redesigned Android application as version 0.3.0-preview.3, versionCode 4, under the LinkGate label with the same non-debuggable package and existing development signing identity.
  Preserve the current Agent Keystore identity and pairing during upgrade; the operator explicitly authorizes uninstalling only the obsolete com.nebula.linkgate application after this upgrade succeeds.
  Keep foreground start/stop private to the owner interface and never expose administrative mutation through Binder or Intent extras.
  Disable backup and keep device keys in Android Keystore; no private-key import/export.
  Advertise only implemented capabilities and require owner startup before business networking.
  Package source-built owned runtimes only from an explicitly selected generated artifact directory, with per-ABI binary hashes; legacy builds without that directory keep runtime capabilities unavailable.
  Keep the API26 direct preview compatible while requiring API29 standard ALPN for authenticated FRP mode.
  Observe default-network changes under the normal network-state permission without changing user network or VPN settings.
